Stop: Jet.ZipLengthMismatch: Zip inputs have different lengths under `strict` policy
  --> Tests/UI/runtime_e0128.jet:9 in run
    |
9 |     loop row in left.zip(right) { print(row.a) }
    |                      ^^^
 Why: Strict `zip` requires every input to end on the same row.
 Fix: Use `zip_short` to intentionally truncate or `zip_pad` to intentionally pad; neither changes strictness automatically.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ZipLengthMismatch
